I am applying for the Senior SAP Developer position at Databricks in Bengalur=
u.

At Black Piano, I build agentic workflows and automated data pipelines. I dev=
eloped a self-healing data-quality agent powered by Gemini that autonomously =
resolves missing brand domains using reference-table lookups with LLM fallbac=
k, retries three times on failure, and escalates via email for human review. =
I also created a custom MCP tool enabling teams to generate publication-ready=
 blog posts from one-line prompts, built an automated market intelligence pip=
eline using ChatGPT APIs, and architected 18 ETL pipelines feeding BigQuery. =
At Pi Software Solutions, I developed production Python data pipelines using =
the internal Pi-API package to automate BigQuery access across dashboards.

Through my independent projects, I design and benchmark autonomous agent arch=
itectures with strict tool calling and scope guardrails. I built MyLocalCLI, =
an open-source terminal coding assistant on npm featuring 42 tools, parallel =
tool dispatch via Promise.all, and an MCP bridge across eight model providers=
. With rAsh Score, I implemented standardized prompt engineering and evaluati=
on harnesses across multiple model APIs alongside text-to-SQL querying. In pr=
ojects like AgentSwarm and BugAgents, I established bounded autonomy, RAG, an=
d hash-chained audit ledgers across thousands of monitored tool calls.

Databricks sets the standard for enterprise data platforms, and I admire your=
 focus on uniting lakehouse infrastructure with production-ready agentic syst=
ems.

I welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in data pipelines, API=
s, and agent engineering can support your team.

